{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "426795c0-91a4-5e3e-ade4-c8116322ab35"/*VolumeNanoVdbCsgExample*/,
  "Description": "A sphere with a box carved out of it, rendered as a NanoVDB liquid surface.\n\n[VolumeCsg] subtracts a box from a sphere. The result goes through [VolumeToNanoVdb] to [NanoVdbRender], which shades the zero level as a reflective surface. A slow noise ripple keeps the surface moving.\n\nAKA: boolean, solid geometry, difference\n\nTips\n- Change the Operation on [VolumeCsg] to Union or Intersection to see the other booleans.",
